; build.ax - the identity of the tree this compiler was built from.
;
; THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES. `axiom version` printed
; `axiom (self-hosted) 0.2.0` and nothing else, so two builds of two
; DIFFERENT trees at one version were indistinguishable to whoever held
; the binary. A version number says what was promised; it does not say
; what was built. `scripts/check-version.sh` has carried that sentence
; in its header since it was written, as the half of the roadmap's P6
; it could not hold.
;
; WHY A LITERAL AND NOT A BUILT-IN. There is no way for a compiler to
; put a build-time value into the binary it produces without a
; mechanism, and every mechanism available here costs something this
; project has priced and refused:
;
;   - a compile-time environment read is a new built-in, and a built-in
;     used by `self_host/` is a construct the committed seed cannot
;     parse - a seed window, and 8.4 MB of regenerated text in the
;     diff, for a string;
;   - a linker-injected symbol is an ungrounded `declare`, which
;     `driver.ax` refuses by name at `AX4004`, and the refusal is
;     right: a freestanding binary that silently gained an undefined
;     symbol is the failure `check-freestanding.sh` exists for;
;   - stamping the ARCHIVE instead of the binary answers for a release
;     and not for the binary, which is the thing that outlives it.
;
; So the value is an ordinary string literal in an ordinary module, and
; `scripts/build-stamped.sh` rewrites it - in a COPY of `self_host/`,
; never in the tree - before building. The seed compiles this file the
; way it compiles any other, the bootstrap ladder never runs the script,
; and `check-bootstrap.sh` and `check-reproducible.sh` see nothing new.
;
; WHY `unstamped` IS NOT A PLAUSIBLE VALUE. An unstamped build has to
; say so in a way no stamped build could be confused with. A build id
; that defaulted to the version, or to a zero hash, or to the empty
; string would read as an answer. This one reads as its own absence,
; and `scripts/check-build-id.sh` asserts that a plain
; `axiom build --input self_host/main.ax` produces exactly it.
; THE VERSION, once. `axiom --help`, `axiom version` and the REPL banner
; all compose "Axiom <version>" from this one literal, so the number
; is stated in exactly one place in the compiler and
; `scripts/check-version.sh` holds that place to `VERSION`.
(pub :: axiomVersion String)

(pub fn (axiomVersion) "0.5.0")

(pub :: axiomBuildId String)

(pub fn (axiomBuildId) "unstamped")
